          { "malayalam": "ശ", "iso15919": "śa", "description": "Palatal fricative. Like 'sh' in 'ship' — tongue near the palate, air passing through.", "isNew": true },
          { "malayalam": "ഷ", "iso15919": "ṣa", "description": "Retroflex fricative. Like 'sh' but with tongue curled back further — a deeper, darker sound.", "isNew": true }
        ],
        "insight": "Both ശ and ഷ produce an 'sh' sound, but at different positions. ശ is at the palate (softer); ഷ is retroflex (tongue curls back). This is the same place distinction as ത/ട and ന/ണ.",
